Z||000036||b lo 0||08-19-2001||11:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by PAUL88GT:<BR><B>If you still want to try to make it work, set up a meeting with her and her pastor.  Then, you may have more insight on some of her statements and ideas. It will help you make your decision on whether or not you should continue the relationship. I hope you get to feeling better.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, I met with her and her pastor over dinner.  That helped a lot.  We are very optimistic about this.  Love hurts sometimes, but when it looks like it's gonna work out, man it feels good!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000037||FieroHeather||08-20-2001||11:45 PM||||Ok...  There has been a LOT that has been said in this post. Coming from a female perspective here, and from someone who has a strong faith, what she said could have been very valid.<P>I love my boyfriend, even though there are things about our faith that differ slightly.  But on the fundamental issues/things, we TOTALLY agree upon them.  There has been many times where he has felt somewhat inadequate for me, due to my schooling background, but I have *never* told him that he was.  I really enjoy listening to him talk about his faith, and I know that if he studied it a little more, he would be a very powerful man of God.  He's got the brain for it--he just doesnt know it (he probably wont read this post anyways, that's why Im saying what I am  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ).  I look at him as my equal, my confident, and my companion.  I dont look down at him whatsoever for ANYTHING.  So what if there is an age difference, a maturity difference, and a label of what our religions are... We love each other and are willing to work on things.  That's what counts.<P>And for the record, two people can be engaged and NOT participate in the horizontal mombo, fyi!  <P>Maybe your girlfriend and yourself should sit down and talk about the fundamentals of your beliefs.  See where the two of you agree and where you may disagree.  This is VERY important.  But dont compromise your fundamental beliefs, for they are part of the very essence of what makes you who you are (unless those fundamental beliefs are totally backwards and in the wrong direction!!)<P>But Im really really happy that the two of you have already started talking, and trying to find some common ground.  I totally *know* where you are coming from b lo O, cause Ive just been there reciently myself (and it is a verrrrry uneasy place to be in).  Enjoy this time to explore who you are, and who the two of you are together.<P>Life is too short... live it while ya can  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000038||JayUSA77||08-22-2001||05:33 PM||||Im glad its working out for you!!! Im still a young man so i dont know what true love is but all i know is when i find it i will try everything in the world to try to hold on to it.  Granted ive had Girlfriends(plural)but none i felt really close to like love. Love is a great thing and it can bring even the strongest man to his knees.  And i think when its time Love will find me but until then PARTY <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> and i was sounding so mature for a while. But that is how i feel. And good for you bLoO hope everything is cool from now on.<BR>j<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000039||b lo 0||08-22-2001||11:50 PM||||Thanks again, guys.  Love is pretty nice.  I would do anything for this to work.  Our date is the day after tomorrow, I'll let yall know how it went, k?||||reg||1
Z||000040||Butter||08-23-2001||03:26 PM||||Let me get this straight now.<P>She worships the god of love but don't practice the emotion of love and you do.<P>She sounds a little hypocritical to me.<P>No disrespect intended.  Love concurs all.<BR>Believe it or leave it.  The church I once belong to (babtist) turned it's back on me during some of my hard times but Jesus did not and some of the members did not.  So I am spiritual but not so inclined to be religious.  If she ever figures that out then she would be more inclined to truely practice what the babtist preaches.  This is just my opinion but it is what I live.  I believe there are many ways to worship God.  By grace through faith we are saved.  Where did it say religion?  I think religion is an avenue to practice your faith.  Being more religious does not necessarily mean you are more faithful. I believe faith comes from the heart and soul.  One day you will loose your heart and be gone from this world, then what is left and where will it go?  I've given my soul to Jesus.  He'll know what to do with it. ||||reg||1
Z||000041||Kasdan||08-24-2001||10:54 PM||||I toally feel yopur pain man.  Im in love with the most perfect girl imagionable, we were together 6 months, had plans of getting married, etc.  I didnt know it was possible to love someone as much as i loved her.  We got along great, its like we were twins, she ahared the same intrests in food, music, movies, tv, cars, etc.  She loved me, and i loved her.  Life was good, i was happy.  I left for 2 weeks, and while im gone, she emails me telling me that shes stopped loving me.  no problem i figure, its because ive been gone for 2 weeks.  I cone back, talk to her every dya, see her almost as much, and she tells me its over, that she stopped liking me.  i know how it feels man, i still love her, i always will.||||reg||13
Z||000042||b lo 0||08-25-2001||12:17 AM||||Hey guys!!!  GREAT news!!  Just got back from our date tonight.  We decided to get back together and work out our differences.  It really felt a lot different tonight, like we understood each other better.  I think in a roundabout way, this was the best thing that has happened for our relationship.  GOSH it felt great to kiss her again.  After a year of seeing (and kissing) her every day, the past week and a half has been like quitting smoking cold-turkey.  I really appreciate all the support and advice, guys.  When I told her how supportive you guys were, she got all emotional.  You guys are a big part of my life, and I appreciate you sharing this important time in my life with me.  I love you guys!   (heard in background: "You're still not getting my Bud Light!")||||reg||1
